title Issue #58, Inventory errors on cart completion: UML Class Diagram

class "POST /store/carts/:id/complete" as Route <<route>> #header:2E7D32;line:2E7D32 {
  - statusOKErrors : string[]
  - <color:#2E7D32><b>statusOKErrorCodes : string[]  (new)</b></color>
  + POST(req, res) : Promise<void>
  <color:#2E7D32><b>  (modified: returns the cart if the error's</b></color>
  <color:#2E7D32><b>   type OR code is in an OK list)</b></color>
}

interface IWorkflowEngineService <<interface>> #header:1F3864 {
  + run(workflowId, { input, throwOnError }) : { errors, result, transaction }
}

class completeCartWorkflow <<workflow>> #header:1F3864 {
  + id = "complete-cart"
}

class reserveInventoryStep <<step>> #header:1F3864 {
  + invoke(items) : ReservationItemDTO[]
  + compensate(reservationIds)
}

class InventoryModuleService <<module service>> #header:2E7D32;line:2E7D32 {
  + createReservationItems(input[]) : ReservationItemDTO[]
  - ensureInventoryLevels(data, { validateQuantityAtLocation })
  <color:#2E7D32><b>  (modified: stock error now passes code</b></color>
  <color:#2E7D32><b>   INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY)</b></color>
}

class MedusaError #header:1F3864 {
  + type : string
  + message : string
  + code? : string
  + {static} Types : MedusaErrorTypes
  + {static} Codes : MedusaErrorCodes
}

Route ..> IWorkflowEngineService : <<use>> resolves from req.scope
IWorkflowEngineService ..> completeCartWorkflow : runs
completeCartWorkflow "1" o-- "1" reserveInventoryStep : contains
reserveInventoryStep ..> InventoryModuleService : <<use>>
InventoryModuleService ..> MedusaError : <<throws>> NOT_ALLOWED\n+ INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY
Route ..> MedusaError : reads type / code

note top of Route
  <b><color:#B8761B>(1) Match by code, not by type</color></b>
  The inventory error is NOT_ALLOWED, but so is the
  promotion limit error from the same workflow. Adding
  NOT_ALLOWED to statusOKErrors would return a cart for
  both, so a separate code list is used.
end note

note right of InventoryModuleService
  <b><color:#B8761B>(2) Tag the error where it starts</color></b>
  ensureInventoryLevels is the only place that knows
  this is a stock problem. It reuses the existing
  INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY code instead of a new error
  type, so the 400 status for other callers (like
  admin reservations) stays the same.
end note

note right of reserveInventoryStep
  <b><color:#B8761B>(3) Aggregation, not composition</color></b>
  The step is shared. Order edits, claims, exchanges
  and draft orders also use it, so it does not
  belong to completeCartWorkflow alone.
end note

note right of IWorkflowEngineService
  <b><color:#B8761B>(4) Dependency, not association</color></b>
  The route resolves the engine from req.scope on
  each request and runs with throwOnError: false,
  so it gets errors back instead of an exception.
end note

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | Navy header | Existing code, unchanged |
  | <back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> Green header </color></back> / <color:#2E7D32><b>green text</b></color> | New or modified for #58 |
  | dashed arrow | Dependency (uses, throws) |
  | hollow diamond | Aggregation (part can exist without whole) |
  | - attr / + method() | Private / public member |
  | <back:#FFF8E6> Amber note </back> | Design decision callout |
endlegend
@enduml
